den progressives win  okay  now up until now I've been saying the  data doesn't seem to confirm that  because in the polls I have been  looking at the top second choice for  Bernie Boat voters has been Biden and  the top second choice for Warren voters  has been Kamala Harris which might seem  surprising because ideologically it  doesn't make sense but along demographic  lines it does make more sense but people  have started sending the recent data  from once again this morning console  poll conducted up until two days ago  ending on September 8th saying David the  numbers have changed Warren voters now  are saying Bernie is their top second  choice it would put Bernie into the lead  if Elizabeth Warren were to drop out but  is this actually what the data says yes  and no let's actually look at it it is  indeed true that in the most recent  morning consult poll the top second  choice for Bernie voters is Joe Biden  and the top second choice of Warren  voters is now Bernie Sanders Elizabeth  Warren voters are now saying more about  Bernie than any other candidate that  elicits if Elizabeth Warren were to drop  out or not be the candidate they would  prefer Bernie Sanders but let's do the  math if Elizabeth Warren were to leave  the race 24% of her support would go to  Bernie 21% would go to Joe Biden and 19%  would go to Kamala Harris and when you  actually look at the numbers if you  divide up Elizabeth Warren's 16  percentage points and consider that only  slightly more of her voters would go to  Bernie than Biden it actually wouldn't  put Bernie in the lead what Elizabeth  Warren dropping out would do on the  basis of second choices in this poll is  it would put Biden at 36% and Bernie at  25% and Kamala Harris at 10% it would  not put Bernie Sanders into the lead her  percentage points 16 percentage points  would go disproportionately a plurality  would go to Bernie Sanders but some  would go to Biden as well and it  wouldn't be enough to put Bernie in the  lead 